course: dictionary
lesson: 14238
title: Finding your way with navigate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Navigate is a word you will meet in many places: maps, history books, ships, and computers. When you meet it, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Sam used a map and a compass to navigate across the forest.» Sam found his way, so navigate means to find the way to a place.
explain: The context can also show you that navigate means steering. «The sailors had no GPS, so they navigated by the stars.» Sailors steer a ship along a route, so navigate can mean to steer. The stars tell you how they found the way.
explain: Navigate can also mean moving safely through difficult things. «She navigated the busy streets safely.» The busy streets are hard to walk through, so navigate here means to get through them carefully. Try your meaning in the sentence, such as «She found her way through the busy streets safely.» If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Navigate means to find the way to a place, using a map, compass, stars or GPS.
fact: Navigate also means to steer a ship, plane or vehicle along a route.
fact: Navigate can mean to move safely through or past difficult things, such as «navigate the busy streets».
fact: On a computer, navigate means to move around a website or app, such as «navigate to the menu».
fact: Navigate can also mean to deal with a hard situation, such as «navigate friendships».
exercise: «Sam used a map and a compass to navigate across the forest.» What does navigate mean here? | Run very fast | *Find the way to a place | Climb to the top of a hill | Fall asleep under a tree
exercise: Explorers in history had no GPS, so they navigated by the stars. What does navigated by the stars mean? | Slept under the stars | *Found their way using the stars | Painted pictures of the stars | Counted the stars for fun
exercise: «Click the link to navigate to the homepage.» What does navigate mean on a computer? | Turn off the computer | *Move around a website or app | Print the page | Draw a picture of the screen
test: «The passenger navigated for the driver, reading the map aloud.» What does navigated mean here? | Drove the car very fast | Slept in the back seat | Washed the windows | *Told the driver which way to go
test: «She had to navigate a hard situation with her best friend.» What does navigate mean? | *Dealt with a difficult problem carefully | Forgot about it at once | Walked around the block | Shouted loudly
exam: Which word is a good swap for navigate when a ship is steered along a route? | Sleep | Jump | Stop | *Steer
